Marcy's annual pension is $50,000/year for the first 40 years. After 20 years, she becomes entitled to 5% of the value of the pension per year. This means that after 20 years, her annual pension will be $50,000/year + 5% of $50,000/year = $50,000/year + $2,500/year = $52,500/year.

If Marcy quits after 30 years, her annual pension will be $52,500/year.

Final answer: \boxed{52,500}
